@startuml sequence-publication-journey
!include elvira.iuml
' What: the catalog is the only component that writes records; every worker gets a task through Redis and reports back to the catalog.
' Source: EvilFlowersCatalog 0.15.0 release notes; READMEs of evilflowers-lcpencrypt-worker, evilflowers-ocr-service, evilflowers-analyzer-service (2026-11-16)
' Scope: one PDF publication. Left out: Redis itself (named on the arrows), storage, the e-mail and statistics side effects.

title One publication, from upload to loan (2026-11)

actor "Librarian" as librarian
participant "EvilFlowersCatalog" as catalog <<focus>>
participant "ocr-service" as ocr
participant "lcpencrypt-worker" as lcp
participant "Readium LCP server" as lcpserver
participant "Extraction workers\nanalyzer · text · image · equation" as extraction
actor "Reader" as reader

librarian -> catalog : upload PDF and metadata\n(portal, REST API, Calibre plugin or MCP)
catalog -> catalog : store record and file

opt Scanned PDF, OCR enabled
  catalog -> ocr : OCR task (Redis)
  ocr -> ocr : add text layer to scanned pages\n(original is kept)
  ocr --> catalog : outcome: new file or skipped
end

opt Title lent with Readium LCP
  catalog -> lcp : encryption task (Redis)
  lcp -> lcpserver : register encrypted file
  lcp --> catalog : report: encrypted, registered
end

opt Extraction enabled, title not lent with LCP
  catalog -> extraction : extraction run (Redis)
  extraction --> catalog : paragraphs, figures, formulas\nPOST /extraction/v1
end

reader -[$accent_msg()]> catalog : <b>borrow</b> /readium/v1
catalog -[$accent_msg()]> lcpserver : <b>issue license</b>
lcpserver --> catalog : license
catalog --> reader : license; open in the portal or an LCP app

caption The catalog is the only writer. Workers take a task from Redis and report back; they never call each other,\nexcept lcpencrypt registering files with the LCP server and the analyzer handing work to the other extraction workers.
@enduml
